<%# THIS APP'S OWN COPY OF turbo-rails' FRAME LAYOUT (2026-10-21), which the gem applies to every
    frame request (Turbo::Frames::FrameRequest) and which this file shadows by path. The gem's carries
    only the CSRF tags in its <head>; this one carries the page's real head (layouts/_head), because a
    frame navigation PROMOTED to a page visit (data-turbo-action="advance") is recorded by Turbo only
    when the response's tracked head elements match the page's. With the gem's, the model page's pane
    advanced the URL while Turbo's lastRenderedLocation stayed on the first one, and Back showed the
    wrong pane (test/system/model_page_test.rb). Turbo reads only the frame out of the body; the head
    costs bytes, not rendering. `lang` is kept because Turbo copies it from the response. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="<%= ui_theme %>">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
